# Test: the schema commands a running daemon serves show an external plugin's module
#
# Question: dispatched by the daemon, do `show schema list` and
# `show yang tree config` answer the module an external plugin declared when
# ze started, and does `show config running` hold the plugin's section?
# Why not a unit test: TestSchemaRegistryHoldsPublishedExternalModule proves
# the registry reads the published set. Only a command the daemon dispatches
# proves boot published the module a live plugin declared before that
# registry was asked. `ze cli -c` cannot prove it: it answers these local-data
# commands in the client process, from the compiled-in modules.
#
# The commands are the ones the daemon has. It serves `show schema list`,
# `methods`, `events`, `handlers` and `protocol`
# (internal/plugins/config-schema/yang/ze-schema-cli-cmd.yang) and no
# `show schema show <module>`, which the daemon answers `unknown command`.
# What the daemon shows of one module is
# its nodes, in `show yang tree config`.
#
# Asserted:
#   - SSH exec of `show schema list` names acme-monitor-conf;
#   - SSH exec of `show yang tree config | json` holds the node acme-monitor
#     with the leaves target and interval, and interval carries the
#     description the module gives it;
#   - `show schema list | match acme-mon` TYPED at the operational prompt of
#     the daemon's session, which is what a `ze cli` session is, names
#     acme-monitor-conf: the route the `ze schema` warning tells an operator
#     to take (externalNotShown, internal/component/config/schema/cli/main.go);
#   - SSH exec of `show config running | json` holds the acme-monitor section.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-13 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup, the schema
#   listing and `show config` half, on the SSH surface.
# PREVENTS: the daemon's schema commands answering compiled-in modules alone
#   while the config it runs holds a section the plugin's module defines; and
#   a warning that names a command the daemon does not know.
#
# Method: the compiled fixture
# (internal/test/fixture/ui_fixture_external_yang_session.go) starts a daemon
# with the external-yang fixture plugin in its valid mode, execs the commands
# over SSH (sshclient.ExecCommand), the route
# test/ui/cli-local-command-daemon-ssh.ci takes, and types one in a session.
#
# The timeout is DECLARED because this file starts a daemon and drives one
# interactive terminal session with a settling window.
option=timeout:value=90s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture ui/external-yang-daemon-schema $PORT
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: the daemon listed acme-monitor-conf, showed its nodes, and its running config holds the acme-monitor section
